{"name":"Herbal Scent","hex":"#8e9b7c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"herbal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made from or with herbs.","Made from natural herbs specifically as opposed to from synthetic materials."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A manual of herbs and their medical uses.","An herbal supplement."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/herbal"},{"term":"scent","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A distinctive smell.","A smell left by an animal that may be used for tracing."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To detect the scent of; to discern by the sense of smell.","To inhale in order to detect the scent of (something)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scent"}],"entries":[{"title":"Herbal","blocks":[{"text":"A herbal is a book containing the names and descriptions of plants, usually with information on their medicinal, tonic, culinary, toxic, hallucinatory, aromatic, or magical powers, and the legends associated with them. A herbal may also classify the plants it describes, may give recipes for herbal extracts, tinctures, or potions, and sometimes include mineral and animal medicaments in addition to those obtained from plants. Herbals were often illustrated to assist plant identification."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Dioscorides_De_Materia_Medica_Byzantium_15th_century.jpg/330px-Dioscorides_De_Materia_Medica_Byzantium_15th_century.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herbal","wikidata":"Q6165948"},{"title":"Odor","blocks":[{"text":"An odor or odour is a smell or a scent caused by one or more volatilized chemical compounds generally found in low concentrations that humans and many animals can perceive via their olfactory system. While smell can refer to pleasant and unpleasant odors, the terms scent, aroma, and fragrance are usually reserved for pleasant-smelling odors and are frequently used in the food and cosmetic industry to describe floral scents or to refer to perfumes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Jan_Brueghel_d._O._-_Allegorie_van_de_geur.jpg/330px-Jan_Brueghel_d._O._-_Allegorie_van_de_geur.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Odor","wikidata":"Q485537"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Teofrasto_Orto_botanico_detail.jpg/500px-Teofrasto_Orto_botanico_detail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Teofrasto_Orto_botanico_detail.jpg/500px-Teofrasto_Orto_botanico_detail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Statue of Theophrastus c. 371 – c. 287 BCE, Orto botanico di Palermo","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATeofrasto_Orto_botanico_detail.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8b/Ebers7766.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8b/Ebers7766.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"A page from the Ebers Papyrus, the most complete and extensive of surviving ancient herbals","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEbers7766.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Arabic_herbal_medicine_guidebook.jpeg/330px-Arabic_herbal_medicine_guidebook.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Arabic_herbal_medicine_guidebook.jpeg/330px-Arabic_herbal_medicine_guidebook.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Arabic Book of Simple Drugs (c. 1334) from Dioscorides’